    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mary Seacole returns two months after her annual wellness visit and six months after her first visit. Her home readings average 126/74 on amlodipine and losartan, with no dizziness on standing and only slight evening ankle swelling. She has had no falls. She walks 20 minutes most days with her cane, goes to tai chi twice a week and to the lunch club, and has lost 2 kg. Her knee pain is 3 out of 10. Her bone density scan showed osteopenia (lowest T-score -1.7 at the left femoral neck) with a 10-year hip fracture risk of 1.4%, below the level at which medicine is advised. Her mammogram, stool test and hepatitis C test were normal. She would like her vaccines today. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home readings</td><td>Average 126/74 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Knees</td><td>Pain 3 out of 10; walking 20 minutes most days</td></tr><tr><td>Screening</td><td>Osteopenia below the treatment threshold; mammogram, stool test and hepatitis C normal</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

