    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertension (I10)</content>. At target: 128/76 in the clinic and 126/74 at home, without an orthostatic drop. Potassium and creatinine were normal at the wellness visit. [S]<list><item>Continue amlodipine 5 mg, losartan 25 mg and atorvastatin 20 mg.</item><item>Metabolic panel and urine albumin in six months; lipids yearly.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Knee osteoarthritis (M17.0)</content>. Pain 3 out of 10; KOOS JR 66.2, up from 52.5. [S]<list><item>Continue tai chi, walking, the gel and her massage.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Obesity, class 1 (E66.811)</content>. 2.6% weight loss so far; the goal is 5%. [S]<list><item>Continue the walking and food changes she has chosen.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk (Z91.81)</content>. No falls in six months; Timed Up and Go 12 seconds. Osteopenia below the treatment threshold. [S]<list><item>Calcium-rich foods and vitamin D from food and sunlight; bone density again in a few years.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure in the clinic (seated, large cuff, two readings) and at home; target below 130/80 mmHg</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>128/76 mmHg; home average 126/74: at target</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Orthostatic blood pressure (lying and standing)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No orthostatic drop</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI (5% weight-loss goal for knee osteoarthritis)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>76.0 kg, BMI 30.8 (2.6% loss)</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Cardiac auscultation and edema</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Trace ankle edema</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Sodium, potassium, creatinine and eGFR</td><td>Two to four weeks after starting or changing a diuretic or ARB; then every six months on these medicines</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Potassium 4.4 mmol/L and creatinine 0.98 mg/dL four weeks after losartan, at the wellness visit; next in six months</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipid panel</td><td>Four to twelve weeks after starting a statin, then yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>LDL 82 mg/dL at the three-month review; next in a year</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio, hemoglobin A1c and TSH</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal six months ago; due in six months</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-9)</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-9 6 at the geriatric assessment; PHQ-2 1 at the wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Knee pain score (0 to 10)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>3 out of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Knee function (KOOS JR)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>KOOS JR 66.2</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Knee examination (range of motion, effusion, alignment, crepitus)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No effusion</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise therapy, tai chi and self-management</td><td>Ongoing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tai chi twice a week; walks 20 minutes most days</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>NSAID safety (topical diclofenac; no oral NSAIDs)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Diclofenac gel only</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>STEADI assessment: Timed Up and Go, 30-second chair stand, 4-stage balance</td><td>At diagnosis of fall risk, then yearly or with a fall</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 12 seconds; no falls</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Bone density (DXA) and fracture risk</td><td>Women 65 and older; repeat by fracture risk</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Osteopenia, lowest T-score -1.7; 10-year hip fracture risk 1.4%, major osteoporotic fracture 8%: no medicine</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Her own remedies: interactions and how she uses them</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Liquorice still paused; ginger tea and liniment</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Loneliness, costs and transport</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tai chi and lunch club; loneliness score improving; costs manageable</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Influenza and other vaccines</td><td>Yearly for influenza</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose influenza vaccine, Tdap and zoster dose 2 today</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg at home and in the clinic, without dizziness on standing. Outcome by 1877-09-14: 128/76 in the clinic and 126/74 at home on amlodipine and losartan, with no orthostatic drop [S]</item><item>Headaches gone. Outcome by 1877-04-13: No headaches since the second week of treatment [S]</item><item>Knee pain 3 or less out of 10 and walking 20 minutes a day with a cane. Outcome by 1877-09-14: Pain 3 out of 10; KOOS JR 52.5 to 66.2; walks 20 minutes most days [S]</item><item>Lose 5% of body weight (about 4 kg). Outcome by 1877-09-14: 78.0 to 76.0 kg (2.6%) [S]</item><item>No falls. Outcome by 1877-09-14: No falls in six months; one near-fall during the sodium problem, without injury [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 2 of 2; Tetanus, diphtheria, and acellular pertussis vaccine (Tdap); Influenza vaccine, high-dose [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025); 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); STEADI: Stopping Elderly Accidents, Deaths, and Injuries (2026); Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024); 2018 AHA/ACC/AACVPR/AAPA/ABC/ACPM/ADA/AGS/APhA/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline on the Management of Blood Cholesterol (2018); Licorice Root (2026); Ginger (2026); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension, osteoarthritis and osteoporosis monographs (2026); Osteoporosis to Prevent Fractures: Screening (2025); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Review in three months; metabolic panel and urine albumin in six months. COVID-19 vaccine this autumn. Call for any fall, dizziness or sudden weakness, numbness or trouble speaking (call 999 at once). [S]</paragraph></text>

